{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "level": 2,
      "ruleId": "classes.ranger",
      "text": "Ranger",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "editorial": true,
      "ruleId": "classes.ranger.roll-drauf-note",
      "text": "This chapter presents the Ranger. Start with the Core Ranger Traits table and the Ranger Features table, then read the class features in level order. The Ranger Spell List names every spell the class can prepare. The Hunter subclass follows at the end.",
      "title": "Roll Drauf reading note",
      "type": "original-note"
    },
    {
      "caption": "Core Ranger Traits",
      "columns": [
        "",
        ""
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Primary Ability",
          "Dexterity and Wisdom"
        ],
        [
          "Hit Point Die",
          "D10 per Ranger level"
        ],
        [
          "Saving Throw Proficiencies",
          "Strength and Dexterity"
        ],
        [
          "Skill Proficiencies",
          "Choose 3: Animal Handling, Athletics, Insight, Investigation, Nature, Perception, Stealth, or Survival"
        ],
        [
          "Weapon Proficiencies Simple and Martial weapons",
          ""
        ],
        [
          "Armor Training",
          "Light and Medium armor and Shields"
        ],
        [
          "Starting Equipment",
          "Choose A or B: (A) Studded Leather Armor, Scimitar, Shortsword, Longbow, 20 Arrows, Quiver, Druidic Focus (sprig of mistletoe), Explorer’s Pack, and 7 GP; or (B) 150 GP"
        ]
      ],
      "ruleId": "classes.ranger.table-1",
      "type": "table"
    },
    {
      "level": 3,
      "ruleId": "classes.ranger.becoming-a-ranger",
      "text": "Becoming a Ranger …",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "level": 4,
      "ruleId": "classes.ranger.becoming-a-ranger.as-a-level-1-character",
      "text": "As a Level 1 Character",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "items": [
        "Gain all the traits in the Core Ranger Traits table.",
        "Gain the Ranger’s level 1 features, which are listed in the Ranger Features table."
      ],
      "ruleId": "classes.ranger.becoming-a-ranger.as-a-level-1-character.list-1",
      "type": "unordered-list"
    },
    {
      "level": 4,
      "ruleId": "classes.ranger.becoming-a-ranger.as-a-multiclass-character",
      "text": "As a Multiclass Character",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "items": [
        "Gain the following traits from the Core Ranger Traits table: Hit Point Die, proficiency with Martial weapons, proficiency in one skill of your choice from the Ranger’s skill list, and training with Light and Medium armor and Shields.",
        "Gain the Ranger’s level 1 features, which are listed in the Ranger Features table. See the multiclassing rules in “Character Creation” to determine your available spell slots."
      ],
      "ruleId": "classes.ranger.becoming-a-ranger.as-a-multiclass-character.list-1",
      "type": "unordered-list"
    },
    {
      "level": 3,
      "ruleId": "classes.ranger.ranger-class-features",
      "text": "Ranger Class Features",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "ruleId": "classes.ranger.ranger-class-features.p-1",
      "text": "As a Ranger, you gain the following class features when you reach the specified Ranger levels. These features are listed in the Ranger Features table.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 4,
      "ruleId": "classes.ranger.ranger-class-features.level-1-spellcasting",
      "text": "Level 1: Spellcasting",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "ruleId": "classes.ranger.ranger-class-features.level-1-spellcasting.p-1",
      "text": "You have learned to channel the magical essence of nature to cast spells. See “Spells” for the rules on spellcasting. The information below details how you use those rules with Ranger spells, which appear in the Ranger spell list later in the class’s description.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "ruleId": "classes.ranger.ranger-class-features.level-1-spellcasting.p-2",
      "text": "Spell Slots. The Ranger Features table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended slots when you finish a Long Rest.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 4,
      "ruleId": "classes.ranger.ranger-class-features.ranger-features",
      "text": "Ranger Features",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "ruleId": "classes.ranger.ranger-class-features.ranger-features.p-1",
      "text": "Proficiency",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "caption": "",
      "columns": [
        "Level",
        "Bonus",
        "Class Features"
      ],
      "rows": [
